load ../correspondence-reuse.maude
--- positive: under an authorized rule, the original's support is reused for
--- both successors
search [1] in CORRESPONDENCE-REUSE : { split(r, r1, r2) accepted(r) support(r) reuseRule proposed(r1) proposed(r2) }
  =>* { derived(r1) derived(r2) RESIDUAL:Cfg } .
--- refusal: without the rule, the correspondence alone carries no support
search in CORRESPONDENCE-REUSE : { split(r, r1, r2) accepted(r) support(r) proposed(r1) proposed(r2) }
  =>* { derived(r1) RESIDUAL:Cfg } .
--- weakening: reuse by resemblance carries it
search [1] in CORRESPONDENCE-REUSE-RESEMBLANCE : { split(r, r1, r2) accepted(r) support(r) proposed(r1) proposed(r2) }
  =>* { derived(r1) RESIDUAL:Cfg } .
--- refusal: reuse, even under the rule, activates nothing
search in CORRESPONDENCE-REUSE : { split(r, r1, r2) accepted(r) support(r) reuseRule proposed(r1) proposed(r2) }
  =>* { active(r1) RESIDUAL:Cfg } .
--- weakening: the transplanting door activates a successor from the split
search [1] in CORRESPONDENCE-REUSE-TRANSPLANT : { split(r, r1, r2) accepted(r) support(r) proposed(r1) proposed(r2) }
  =>* { active(r1) RESIDUAL:Cfg } .
--- positive: an admitted activation act activates the successor it names, and
--- only that one
search [1] in CORRESPONDENCE-REUSE : { split(r, r1, r2) accepted(r) proposed(r1) proposed(r2) activation(r1) }
  =>* { active(r1) proposed(r2) RESIDUAL:Cfg } .
--- refusal: the act for one successor never activates the other
search in CORRESPONDENCE-REUSE : { split(r, r1, r2) accepted(r) proposed(r1) proposed(r2) activation(r1) }
  =>* { active(r2) RESIDUAL:Cfg } .
--- positive: a previously authorized policy performs the act, and the act is
--- what activates
search [1] in CORRESPONDENCE-REUSE : { split(r, r1, r2) accepted(r) proposed(r1) proposed(r2) autoActivate }
  =>* { activation(r1) RESIDUAL:Cfg } .
search [1] in CORRESPONDENCE-REUSE : { split(r, r1, r2) accepted(r) proposed(r1) proposed(r2) autoActivate }
  =>* { active(r1) active(r2) RESIDUAL:Cfg } .
quit .
